---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { ShieldCheck } from "lucide-react";
---

<Layout title="Privacy">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
    <div class="mb-8 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-16 h-16 bg-amber-400 rounded-2xl shadow-inner mb-4">
        <ShieldCheck className="w-8 h-8 text-stone-900" strokeWidth={2.5} />
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-stone-100">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-stone-400 text-sm mt-1 font-medium">How we look after your data and your memories</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-stone-900 rounded-2xl border border-stone-800 p-6 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-400">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-extrabold text-stone-100 mb-1.5">What we store</h2>
        <p>
          Your email, username, and password (handled by Supabase Auth — we never see it in plain
          text), and whatever you upload: photos, videos, titles, descriptions, and memory dates.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-extrabold text-stone-100 mb-1.5">How your files are kept safe</h2>
        <p>
          Each photo or video is stored in a per-user folder, protected by row-level security (RLS)
          policies: only you can upload or delete inside your own folder, and access credentials
          always travel encrypted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-extrabold text-stone-100 mb-1.5">Who can see your memories</h2>
        <p>
          Right now, memories you upload are visible to anyone who visits the platform — it's built
          to be shared within the family. We don't sell your data or share it with third parties
          for commercial purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-extrabold text-stone-100 mb-1.5">Services we use</h2>
        <p>
          We host the database and files on Supabase, and publish the site on Netlify. Neither uses
          your data for advertising.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
